WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.120
You join me today in ancient Greece.

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:04.640
It's-
- (Well- this)

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:06.879
(doesn't look like it. 
They've good lighting.)

00:00:06.879 --> 00:00:09.120
Thanks, it's it's not not what you were

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.080
expecting but it's 6th century BC

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:14.240
and in particular we're on a Greek

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:16.080
island just off the coast of Turkey. It's

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.400
called Samos and,

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:19.520
I know what you're thinking, you'd like

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:20.960
to dig a tunnel through a mountain,

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:23.039
wouldn't you?

00:00:23.039 --> 00:00:24.880
Question is how on Earth do you dig a

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:26.800
tunnel through a mountain when you don't

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:29.599
have access to any modern equipment?

00:00:29.599 --> 00:00:31.599
I'll tell you how you dig a tunnel

00:00:31.599 --> 00:00:34.559
through a mountain! Okay so here is your

00:00:34.559 --> 00:00:36.079
mountain,

00:00:36.079 --> 00:00:38.399
lovely. Now there are a couple of things

00:00:38.399 --> 00:00:40.079
that you need to dig a tunnel through a

00:00:40.079 --> 00:00:42.239
mountain: you're going to need to have an

00:00:42.239 --> 00:00:45.039
entrance and an exit, those are

00:00:45.039 --> 00:00:47.760
the two requisite components of a tunnel.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:50.480
So let's say you want to go in here

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.399
and you want to come out here.

00:00:52.399 --> 00:00:54.160
Now the thing is is that you can't just

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:56.719
start digging in here and just

00:00:56.719 --> 00:00:58.559
hope that you'll come out here, it's not

00:00:58.559 --> 00:01:00.559
gonna work right? You need to make sure

00:01:00.559 --> 00:01:01.920
that you hit the right bit. So what

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:03.280
people tend to do - this is what they did

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:05.280
for the channel tunnel for example -

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:07.600
is you start digging here and you start

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.760
digging here and you just hope that they

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:11.360
line up.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:13.439
Except that- I mean- you you're

00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:14.880
unlikely to find each other in the

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.640
middle of a mountain.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:19.520
So you need a technique to make sure

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:22.000
that these two lines end up meeting up

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.000
in the middle. And the way that you do

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:27.360
that is by using triangles.

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:28.720
(I would have thought if you made)

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:30.799
(absolutely sure you were digging in a)

00:01:30.799 --> 00:01:32.400
(straight line)

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:33.840
(you'd be all right.)

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:35.280
(As long as you can 
always- as long as you)

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:37.280
(look behind you and the hole)

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:38.640
(is still behind you- )
- Yeah but the

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:41.040
straight line- Hang on, if you were in a

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:42.320
straight line, okay so let's imagine that

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:44.720
you- let me do like a contour of this

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:45.920
mountain.

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:48.159
It's quite a wobbly mountain this one. So

00:01:48.159 --> 00:01:50.000
you want to go in here and you want to

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.920
come out here; the problem is that if you

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:53.759
dig in a straight line you could end up

00:01:53.759 --> 00:01:55.840
over here.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:57.520
(Right, so how do you make sure- )
- How do you make

00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:59.520
sure that you get exactly there?

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:00.880
And it's not like you can just stand on

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:02.320
the top of the mountain and you go,

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:04.399
heading that way lads.

00:02:04.399 --> 00:02:05.600
You know what I mean? Because you can't-

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:06.719
when you're standing over here you can't

00:02:06.719 --> 00:02:08.530
see around there.
- (Right)

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:11.680
So it's really hard to even- to even know.
(I feel like in)

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.000
(the era of GPS you could just do the)

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.599
(straight line.)
- In GPS I think you

00:02:15.599 --> 00:02:17.840
probably can. I think you probably can.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:18.879
Apart from the fact that you're in a

00:02:18.879 --> 00:02:20.480
tunnel, I don't think signal's great in

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:22.800
tunnels but-

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:24.560
(If you start in a straight line and then)

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:26.000
(just keep looking behind you to make)

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.599
(sure that the hole's still there, you)

00:02:27.599 --> 00:02:29.440
(know you're going in a straight line.)

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:30.879
(Anyway.)

00:02:30.879 --> 00:02:32.959
(So you're saying the main problem is you)

00:02:32.959 --> 00:02:34.959
(can't see the other side?)
- You can't see

00:02:34.959 --> 00:02:36.879
where you're going, yeah, exactly.

00:02:36.879 --> 00:02:38.879
So the way that you do this,

00:02:38.879 --> 00:02:40.400
it's very neat.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.360
So you try and walk around from one side

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:45.599
of the mountain to the other, and as you

00:02:45.599 --> 00:02:47.440
go - you want to try and stay at the same

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:49.360
level as you go around - every time you

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:51.840
take a step south you add it up, every

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:54.800
time you take a step to the

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:57.680
west you add up, and you're very careful

00:02:57.680 --> 00:02:59.280
about how big all of your steps are as

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:00.800
you're going.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:02.959
Maybe you do this twice just to make

00:03:02.959 --> 00:03:04.959
sure you've got the right numbers. You've

00:03:04.959 --> 00:03:06.959
done it all in units and right angles

00:03:06.959 --> 00:03:08.560
and you've been really careful all the

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:10.800
way along; because even in ancient Greece

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:12.159
you can imagine it'd be quite easy to

00:03:12.159 --> 00:03:13.760
construct a right angle, wouldn't be too

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:16.959
difficult. But in total then, imagine that

00:03:16.959 --> 00:03:21.120
you have taken 84 steps west and you

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:24.159
have taken 13 steps south. So effectively

00:03:24.159 --> 00:03:27.120
then to get the direction from one place

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:29.280
to the other you are talking about a

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:30.640
triangle

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:33.280
with those as the sides, so you know it's

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:36.480
going to be 84 along there and 13 along

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:38.080
there, and you know that that's a right

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:40.080
angle because you've only ever walked

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:43.360
south and west. And so you have this very

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:45.360
nice neat triangle - I deliberately chose

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:47.280
one that was a Pythagorean triple, you're

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:50.666
welcome - so this is 85.

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:54.640
So now actually when you are at the

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:56.959
entrance to each of these tunnels

00:03:56.959 --> 00:03:59.120
you can construct a much smaller version

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:01.760
of the same triangle and build it here.

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:03.599
And if you make a kind of really long

00:04:03.599 --> 00:04:06.720
rod to sort of extend that angle, and you

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:08.239
do the same thing over here so you've

00:04:08.239 --> 00:04:10.480
got another version of the triangle here,

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:12.640
then you should have

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:14.879
these two lines- these two angles that

00:04:14.879 --> 00:04:17.299
will meet really perfectly in the middle.

00:04:20.799 --> 00:04:22.320
So the only thing you've got to be

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:23.680
careful of now

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:25.759
is when you're digging

00:04:25.759 --> 00:04:27.120
to make sure that you stay perfectly

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:28.240
flat, you don't want to go up you don't

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:29.440
want to go down.

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:31.040
And the way that they do that is that

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:33.520
they put water in the tunnel,

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:35.360
and then as they're digging they make

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:37.440
sure that the water just sits nice and

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:39.600
still rather than dripping in one

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:41.640
direction or the other.
- (Like a spirit level?)

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.680
Like a spirit level, exactly. This

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:46.960
particular mountain, this is Samos and

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:49.930
this was in 525 BC.

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:53.040
Polycrates - I don't think he's called

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:55.199
Polycrates-

00:04:55.199 --> 00:04:57.490
'How do you pronounce Poly-crates?'

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:00.400
[Computer: Poly-crit-ees]

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:02.880
Oh it's Polycrates- whatever, Polycrates

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:05.120
he wanted a tunnel.

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:07.120
You can- you can shush. Polycrates he

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:10.720
wanted this tunnel; it's a kilometer long,

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:13.520
525 BC this was built and this is exactly

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:15.360
the technique that archaeologists think

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:16.720
that they used.

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:19.520
And when they did so they did incredibly

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:21.120
well. There was a tiny bit of zigzagging

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.960
at one end, and they think it was because

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:24.000
they were trying to work their way

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:26.000
around some quite difficult rock, but

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.680
then they re-established this sort of

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:29.680
plum line as it were. And when these two

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:32.080
tunnels met in the middle, 
there's like a tiny

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:34.479
little step of 60 centimeters. It's like

00:05:34.479 --> 00:05:36.960
this unbelievably remarkable achievement

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:38.960
with just some triangles.

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:40.639
(How do you know where to put those)

00:05:40.639 --> 00:05:42.479
(triangles so the triangles are at the)

00:05:42.479 --> 00:05:45.280
(right-)
- That's got to be a line that runs

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:46.479
exactly

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:48.160
east to west, and that's got to be a line

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:50.560
that runs exactly north to south.

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:52.639
Do they have compasses?

00:05:52.639 --> 00:05:54.000
I'm assuming they had compasses.
- (Well)

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.680
(they knew- they had the sun.)
- They had the

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:58.400
sun yeah, yeah that's true. Your

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:00.880
open and close to the tunnel, they

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:02.960
actually need to be at the same level

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:04.320
before you start. You know the water-

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:06.479
(At the same altitude?)
- Yeah the same altitude, exactly.

00:06:06.479 --> 00:06:07.759
Your water thing wouldn't work if you

00:06:07.759 --> 00:06:09.280
had one of your- if you're like yeah yeah

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:10.560
let's start there and you hadn't worked

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:12.000
out that actually one was much more

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.440
uphill than the other. Now this is

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:15.360
something they're not quite sure about

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:17.759
how they did it, how they managed it, but

00:06:17.759 --> 00:06:20.479
there is some suggestion - I think it's

00:06:20.479 --> 00:06:22.639
I'm not convinced by this - but there's

00:06:22.639 --> 00:06:24.880
some suggestions some archaeologists

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:26.720
think that created this tower and then

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:30.160
got a massive long stick.

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:33.680
I mean,

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:35.680
maybe I haven't understood this quite

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:38.319
right, but my understanding of it is they

00:06:38.319 --> 00:06:39.600
went up to the top of the tower and then

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:41.840
they dangled a big long stick down and

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:43.440
then they sort of swung it around the

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:45.440
mountain. So they were like, oh there you

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:48.000
go, that's a nice point right there.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:49.840
(Well you could use a rope
for that surely)

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:52.240
And make it straight? Yeah. 
- (Like taut,)

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:54.080
(although it's pretty hard to keep a rope)

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:55.440
(that long taut.)
- Yeah it's like a

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:56.800
kilometer.

00:06:56.800 --> 00:06:58.319
But I don't think they built a kilometer

00:06:58.319 --> 00:06:59.919
long stick either.

